", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_riskpremiaingoldleasingmarkets": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_risksharingwithinfirmsworldwideevidence": {"abstract": "Using a firm -level international panel dataset, we study if unemployment insurance offered by the government and by firms are substitutes. We exploit cross-country and time-series variation in public unemployment insurance as a shifter of workers\u2019 demand for insurance within firms , and family vs. non-family ownership as a shifter of firms \u2019 supply of insurance. Our evidence supports the substitutability hypothesis: employment stability in family firms is greater, and the wage discount larger, in countries and periods with less generous public unemployment insurance, while no such substitutability emerges for non-family firms .", "source": "ideas_snippet_10o"}, "afa_2014_tailriskandhedgefundreturns": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_theendofmarketdisciplineinvestorexpectat": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_theexternalitiesofcrowdedtrades": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_theexternalitiesofhighfrequencytrading": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_themicrostructureoftheeuropeansovereignb": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whatdriveswomenoutofentrepreneurshipthej": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whatistheimpactoffinancialadvisorsonreti": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whenshareholderapprovalmatters20percentr": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whenthecongresssayspipyourkerpperformanc": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whydogovernmentslendevidencefromthecorpo": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whydoinvestorstrade": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2014_whydouniversityendowmentsinvestsomuchinr": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2015_dofraudulentfirmsengageindisclosureherdi": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2015_dotakeoverlawsmatterevidencefrom45yearso": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2015_harne