risk . Empirically, we find that in firms with weak cash flow prospects, fund holding shares increase CDS spreads, and more so when flows are more sensitive to performance.", "source": "ideas_snippet_10o"}, "afa_2022_didwesternceoincentivescontributetochina": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_financialimplicationsofdisenfranchisemen": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_howharmfulisinsidertradingforoutsidersev": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_inequalitydiscriminationandthefinancials": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_investingincrises": {"abstract": "We investigate asset returns around banking crises in 44 advanced and emerging economies from 1960 to 2018. In contrast to the view that buying assets during banking crises is a profitable long-run strategy, we find returns of equity and other asset classes generally underperform after banking crises . While prices are depressed during crises and partially recover after acute stress ends, consistent with theories of fire sales and intermediary-based asset pricing, we argue that investors do not fully anticipate the consequences of debt overhang, which result in lower long-run dividends.", "source": "ideas_snippet_10o"}, "afa_2022_investorprotectionsandstockmarketpartici": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_jointdeterminationofcounterpartyandliqui": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_learningfromprospectuses": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_lockedinathomelimitedattentionoffemalean": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_obsoletefirms": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_ontheoriginofipoprofits": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_performancepayandrisksharingbetweenfirms": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_presentedby": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_psychologicaldistanceanddeviationsfromra": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_sectorallaborreallocationandreturnpredic": {"abstract": "", "source": ""}, "afa_2022_theheterog